{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793485601329729001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"doglike-gossipy-pussycat","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":4},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Two more cases, from 2a3d-9d00's re-review at d74d53a5ffd. Both dropped under veto:cited-reference-inaccurate, both verified correct against the tree. That makes 5 of 5 checked drops wrong, across three tickets (c159 x2, 2a3d x2, 28d0 x1).\n\nCase 4 — finding: plan cites 'AGENTS.md:215,428' as the lines already referencing the packaged guides. Measured on origin/main d74d53a5ffd: writing-a-passing-plan.md is cited at AGENTS.md:225 and passing-code-review.md at :443. The finding's own correction (:225, :443) was exact. Dropped anyway.\n\nCase 5 — finding: plan cites 'registry.py:665-666' as naming the packaged basenames. Measured: the AUTHOR_GUIDES entries are at src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py:615-616. The plan also gave a bare filename where the repo has two candidate paths, which the finding noted. Dropped anyway.\n\nBoth strengthen the hypothesis in the description: the veto appears to compare the finding's cited location against the plan's cited location and read the mismatch as the FINDING being inaccurate, when the mismatch is exactly what a correct finding about a wrong citation looks like. It fires precisely when the plan is wrong, which is when the finding is most needed.\n\nSample now: 5 drops checked, 5 correct, 0 incorrect. No case has yet been found where the veto suppressed a genuinely inaccurate finding.","timestamp":1793477244004356001}],"created_at":1793476100235287001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"3789ae5b-b4e1-4974-8e89-e340250ed2e2","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c159-1621-c2a6-4385"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe plan-review gate's `veto:cited-reference-inaccurate` check dropped three findings across two reviews on 2026-10-31. All three were verified against the tree afterwards and all three were CORRECT. The veto has a 0/3 precision record on the cases checked.\n\nCase 1 — story 28d0-148d-43a6-4e5e, review at verified_at_sha d74d53a5ffd. Finding f49e9d9ad9502c56e (G1G2) said the plan cites `tests/unit/test_init_ensures_seam.py`, which does not exist. Verified: `git grep -l init_ensures_seam` returns nothing repo-wide and the path does not exist. The plan cited it twice, once in Context as the pin for `init._<name>` reachability and once in Testing as a pytest target, so running the plan's own verification would have errored on a nonexistent path. Dropped as veto:cited-reference-inaccurate.\n\nCase 2 — story c159-1621-c2a6-4385, same sha. The finding said the plan's `CHANGELOG.md:371` for the REBAR_LLM_MODEL v0.12.0 removal is mis-measured. Verified: :371 is issue_count prose; the `## [0.12.0] - 2026-08-15` heading is at :543 and the removal at :569. The plan's citation was also internally impossible, since :371 precedes the heading it claimed to sit under.\n\nCase 3 — same review. The finding said `docs/release-notes.md:84-91` and `CHANGELOG.md:65-75` are mis-measured for the 0092 reconcile-compatibility removal. Verified: :84-91 is the REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS tombstone, CHANGELOG :65-75 is REBAR_HLC plus 429 retry, and the real anchors are docs/release-notes.md:833 and CHANGELOG.md:213.\n\n## The suspected mechanism\n\nThe pattern in all three is identical: the finding's subject IS a citation in the plan, and the finding's evidence contains the corrected location. If the veto compares the finding's cited location against the plan's cited location and treats a mismatch as the finding being inaccurate, then it fires exactly when the plan is wrong — inverting its purpose. A mis-cited plan is precisely the condition the finding exists to report, so the veto is strongest where it should be silent.\n\nThis is a hypothesis about the mechanism, not a verified root cause; the veto's implementation has not been read.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nBoth reviews returned PASS with 0 blocking while carrying real, correctable plan defects. In case 1 the defect was a broken verification oracle that would have failed at implementation time. A PASS verdict that suppresses accurate citation findings makes the gate weaker precisely on the defect class the pre-sweep discipline keeps catching by hand.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The veto's decision rule is read and documented, establishing whether a mismatch between the finding's location and the plan's location is what triggers it.\n- [ ] A regression test reproduces case 1: a plan citing a nonexistent test path, with a G1G2 finding naming the real path, is NOT dropped by the veto.\n- [ ] Re-running review-plan on a fixture built from case 2 or case 3 surfaces the citation finding instead of dropping it.\n- [ ] The three cases above are either surfaced as findings or the veto's continued suppression of them is justified in the ADR or criteria guide with reasoning that addresses all three.\n\n## Testing\n`pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review.py` plus whichever module pins the veto table; identify it with `git grep -ln 'cited-reference-inaccurate'`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_id":"1d00-91dd-23a2-4933","ticket_type":"bug","title":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate drops correct findings when the PLAN's citation is the inaccurate one","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["85fcdbe8-650d-4930-9477-5a0b37212693","3789ae5b-b4e1-4974-8e89-e340250ed2e2","6e70e956-c960-4821-925e-19e28b409b91","020f7587-751a-47ee-aa92-e136e912030d"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793485601329729001,"uuid":"4719b491-3e03-4d50-80fc-9a93adfc5e00"}